WEBVTT

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:07.540
Miss Fiene? What is the meaning of this?

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:13.290
Why are you all alone with my fiancé,
His Highness Prince Siegwald?

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:18.080
Well, uh... it's just...

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:20.250
I didn't understand something in class, so-

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:22.040
I suppose a commoner like yourself

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:26.170
would find it difficult keeping up with
the lectures here at the Academy of Magic.

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:30.250
Perhaps I could offer some instruction as well.

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:36.290
Or could it be you only wish to accept
advice from dashing young gentlemen?

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:41.750
O-of course not...

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:43.040
Lieselotte...

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:48.000
So strong with the tsun!

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:48.670
Huh?

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:52.130
Coming on so strong with the tsun, Lieselotte!

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:53.630
A voice...?

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:58.000
By that, I think Lieselotte just
wanted to say "let me join you,"

00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:00.380
but it really didn't come across that way at all!

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:04.380
The two voices that began coming
from the heavens at this point

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:10.580
were those of the two venerable divine entities
who would later go down in our kingdom's history

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:14.670
as Endoh the Running Commentator
and Kobayashee the Expert Analyst.

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:50.290
It's just, the best of the best otome games ever!

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:53.830
Love Me Magically!, also known as Magikoi!

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:55.080
<b>Chapter 1</b>

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:55.080
<b>The Tsundere, the Prince, and the Voices of the Gods</b>

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:55.290
We gotta play it today! Please?

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:56.290
C'mon, Endo!

00:02:57.170 --> 00:02:58.170
Uh...

00:02:58.290 --> 00:02:59.960
Okay, but...

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:03.670
It's set in a post-medieval European-style
fantasy world where magic exists!

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:08.920
The commoner girl Fiene finds out she can use magic
even though it's a skill exclusive to the aristocracy,

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:13.330
<b>The</b>

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:13.330
<b>Royal</b>

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:13.330
<b>Academy</b>

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:13.330
<b>of Magic</b>

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:13.040
and our story starts with her getting admitted
to the Royal Academy of Magic.

00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:20.330
<b>The Royal Academy of Magic</b>

00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:15.330
<b>Fiene</b>

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:15.330
<b>Hello, my name is Fiene!</b>

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:19.420
Once there, Fiene meets a whole slew of gorgeous guys!

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:15.330
<b>It's very nice to meet you!</b>

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:20.330
<b>Say hello to the most handsome faces the academy has to offer!!</b>

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:23.170
And so, she falls in love...

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:25.170
swoons...

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:27.330
swoons again...

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:29.330
and again...!

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:33.330
...and goes on an adventure or two in the meantime.

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:34.290
But really,

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:39.080
the most important thing about
Magikoi is that Lieselotte's in it!

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:44.960
You see, Liese-tan is beautiful and excels at
everything—an ultra-high-spec lady villainess!

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:47.630
She always seems to be chastising Fiene...

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:53.130
...but she's actually valiant and devoted,
and really just a tsundere when it comes down to it.

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:55.000
E-Endo!

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.380
So you finally played Magikoi?!

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:01.420
Uh, no. You've been telling me every single day, so...

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:02.330
Aww.

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:05.250
Oh, are you busy trying to spread your obsession again?

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:05.750
Hey!

00:04:06.130 --> 00:04:07.330
Hello, everyone.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.460
Come on, help me out here, Prez!

00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:12.330
Hmm? I guess.

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:15.290
Endo, I think you should give Magikoi a try.

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:15.880
See?!

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:18.880
Or else this one will keep pestering you forever!

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:20.330
F-forever...?

00:04:20.330 --> 00:04:21.880
Uh, I wouldn't go that far...

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:23.580
Here, found it.

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:24.880
Ah, wonderful!

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:27.500
But seriously, this club...

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:29.920
It's so lax.

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:35.630
Being lax is the greatest of virtues! That's us,
the Hanahashi Ikuei High School Broadcasting Club!

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:36.460
Okay...

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:37.420
However!

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:40.460
The broadcast when school ends for the day
is the one thing we have to do.

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:42.670
You two are in charge today!

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:43.790
Oh, right!

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:46.330
Other than that, go ahead and do whatever you wish.

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:58.460
So anyway, let's play Magikoi!

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:02.960
Otome games are mostly for girls, though. I dunno...

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:06.920
Don't worry! Magikoi has the power
to move any person alive.

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:11.750
B...but I was late joining the club,
so I really should practice my diction and stuff.

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:13.710
Ahhh!

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:14.920
Whoa, what's up?

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:16.750
Endo, that's it!

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:17.460
Huh?

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:20.290
Why don't you do a running commentary
while playing Magikoi?!

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:21.420
"A running commentary"?

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:22.500
Yes, exactly!

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:26.580
It'll be a good diction exercise, and great practice
for school-wide tournaments and stuff!

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:27.170
Okay...

00:05:27.170 --> 00:05:29.170
Yeah, that's great! A great idea!

00:05:29.170 --> 00:05:31.080
I can handle the analysis, then!

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:32.380
I'll do the commentary?

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:33.210
Mm-hm.

00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:34.420
And you'll analyze?

00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:35.250
Mm-hm!

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:39.080
Just like a baseball broadcast,
with running commentary and expert analysis!

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:43.210
<b>Siegwald</b>

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:43.210
<b>Fitzenhagen</b>

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:45.630
<b>Baldur</b>

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:45.630
<b>Riefenstahl</b>

00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:47.960
<b>Artur</b>

00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:47.960
<b>Richter</b>

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:50.460
<b>Fabian</b>

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:50.460
<b>Oltenberg</b>

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:52.830
<b>Leon Schach</b>

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:55.330
<b>Fiene</b>

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:00.290
<b>Love Me</b>

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:00.290
<b>Magically!</b>

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:02.540
I'll put it on autoplay mode.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:04.460
So it'll be easier to do the commentary.

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:05.040
Okay.

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:08.250
Endo's cheered up a lot, huh?

00:06:08.580 --> 00:06:09.710
Yeah.

00:06:10.170 --> 00:06:13.710
When he joined our club halfway through the year
he was still pretty bummed out.

00:06:13.710 --> 00:06:15.290
It's all thanks to Kobayashi, huh?

00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:17.750
Endo should just confess his feelings already.

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:20.540
Well, that depends on how
Kobayashi feels about him, right?

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:27.250
Well, whatever the case, we'll do the wingman thing
and pair them up whenever we can.

00:06:27.250 --> 00:06:29.040
Hey, right there. It's getting burned.

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:29.790
Hmm?

00:06:29.790 --> 00:06:30.790
Whoops! Ooh, that's hot!

00:06:32.130 --> 00:06:34.000
I think we should start around here.

00:06:34.670 --> 00:06:37.880
The lunch break scene with Fiene,
the new girl who everyone's talking about!

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:38.920
O-okay...

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:50.330
<b>The Royal Academy of Magic—Dining Hall</b>

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:46.130
It's starting!

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:50.330
<b>Fiene</b>

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:50.330
<b>I'm so nervous…</b>

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:48.500
Okay, the commentary goes first. Go!

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:49.580
R-right...

00:06:50.790 --> 00:06:56.330
Ah, here comes our heroine, Fiene,
as she enters the dining hall. She looks a little anxious.

00:06:56.580 --> 00:07:00.250
Although her abilities in magic got her a place
at the academy despite being a commoner,

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:02.330
everyone else is part of the aristocratic elite.

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:05.460
A true social outcast. This has got to be distressing.

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:07.920
Endo, your commentary's sounding great!

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:09.670
I can't believe this is your first go at this!

00:07:09.670 --> 00:07:10.830
Y-you really think so?

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:13.250
Oh look! Here comes a handsome face!

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:18.080
That's Baldur! Liese-tan's cousin, a diligent
and skilled warrior who's also a great guy.

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:20.880
You must be Fiene. My name is Baldur.

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:23.830
If you're unsure about anything, feel free to ask.

00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:25.380
Thank you very much.

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:27.830
So that's the Fiene everyone's talking about?

00:07:27.830 --> 00:07:30.330
Hmm? What's an elementary school kid doing here?

00:07:30.330 --> 00:07:31.710
That's Fabian.

00:07:31.710 --> 00:07:35.540
A genius with magic, he gained
special admittance to the academy

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:38.380
to learn how to control his overwhelming amount of
power.

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:42.710
But he's a difficult character to win over
that requires the player to actively pursue him.

00:07:42.710 --> 00:07:43.540
I see.

00:07:43.750 --> 00:07:46.540
A commoner who can use magic, hmm?

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:49.500
Oh, and now in stark contrast is a grownup character!

00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:50.880
Professor Leon!

00:07:51.130 --> 00:07:56.080
He's a powerful user of magic who hides his abilities
and generally keeps everyone at a distance.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:58.040
A very difficult character to win over.

00:07:58.330 --> 00:08:00.830
But that's also what makes him so appealing!

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:01.630
Huh.

00:08:01.630 --> 00:08:04.960
Ooh! There he is, our main hero, Siegwald!

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:06.330
<b>The Royal Academy of Magic—Dining Hall</b>

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:06.330
<b>Siegwald</b>

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:06.330
<b>I'm the student council president, Siegwald.</b>

00:08:03.590 --> 00:08:06.330
<b>Feel free to ask if you need help with anything.</b>

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:05.960
That's him?

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:12.580
I'm the student council president, Siegwald.
Feel free to ask if you need help with anything.

00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:14.580
Oh, thank you so much.

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:18.540
Ooh, now there's a prince if I ever saw one!

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:22.290
He's the crown prince of the kingdom and
the academy's student council president!

00:08:22.290 --> 00:08:24.580
The main love interest for the player to win over!

00:08:24.790 --> 00:08:27.080
U-um actually...

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:27.960
What is it?

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:30.670
There's something I didn't understand in class.

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:34.460
Oh, sure.

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:38.080
Just look at that princely smile!

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:40.790
Who wouldn't fall for that?

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:43.630
By the way, aren't there supposed
to be five potential suitors?

00:08:43.630 --> 00:08:47.250
Oh. Artur doesn't appear yet in this scene.

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:50.540
Art is a priest who serves the Goddess Lirenna,

00:08:50.540 --> 00:08:55.130
and he's absent at the moment because he's off helping
with some disaster recovery in the western regions.

00:08:55.130 --> 00:08:56.170
I see.

00:09:02.420 --> 00:09:04.880
So, what exactly do you need help with?

00:09:05.290 --> 00:09:08.170
Well, there's this part in the study of Magical Theory...

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:08.880
Hmm?

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:16.080
This, right here.

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:17.630
Oh, that part.

00:09:20.630 --> 00:09:23.130
So if that's the case, what's the answer?

00:09:23.130 --> 00:09:24.170
Oh. I see!

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:26.920
Exactly, you're quite the fast learner.

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:31.420
A-am I? Thank you very much. I really get it now.

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:32.580
Oh, and also-

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:33.920
My, what have we here?

00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:37.420
What exactly are you doing here with the crown prince,

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:39.170
Miss Fiene?

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:41.880
Oh, um...

00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:49.330
What is the meaning of this? Why are you all alone
with my fiancé, His Highness Prince Siegwald?!

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:53.960
Yesss! There she is! Liese-tan makes her entrance!

00:09:55.330 --> 00:09:58.080
Well, I didn't understand something in class, so...

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:00.540
Liselotte, what brings you here?

00:10:00.540 --> 00:10:06.960
A thoughtful someone kindly informed me that my fiancé
was spending time alone with a certain young woman.

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:10.920
She was having trouble, so I simply offered
to help as student council president.

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:14.420
There's absolutely nothing for you to worry about.

00:10:17.670 --> 00:10:19.670
I suppose a commoner like yourself

00:10:19.670 --> 00:10:23.380
would find it difficult keeping up with
the lectures here at the Academy of Magic.

00:10:23.710 --> 00:10:27.330
Perhaps I could offer some instruction as well.

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:32.790
Or could it be you only wish to accept
advice from dashing young gentlemen?

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:35.130
O-okay, wow...!

00:10:36.380 --> 00:10:37.460
So strong...

00:10:37.630 --> 00:10:38.630
with the tsun!

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:52.880
So strong. Coming on so strong with the tsun, Lieselotte!

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:54.170
A voice...?

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:59.040
By that, I think Lieselotte just
wanted to say "let me join you,"

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:01.040
but it really didn't come across that way at all!

00:11:01.040 --> 00:11:03.790
Why would you do that, Lieselotte?!

00:11:03.790 --> 00:11:05.290
How do you not understand that

00:11:05.290 --> 00:11:07.750
being passive aggressive like that is
just going to push His Highness away?!

00:11:07.920 --> 00:11:10.210
Well, Lieselotte's your typical tsundere!

00:11:10.330 --> 00:11:12.210
She's not capable of saying how she really feels.

00:11:12.210 --> 00:11:17.710
Like how she's sincerely worried that Fiene's
reputation will suffer from her ignorant behavior...

00:11:18.540 --> 00:11:20.080
No one else hears this?

00:11:22.670 --> 00:11:23.540
Your Highness?

00:11:23.540 --> 00:11:28.380
...or that she's so hopelessly in love with
His Highness that she can't help being jealous!

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:32.460
"In love"? Who? With whom?

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:34.380
Besides, what is a "tsun de rais"?

00:11:34.830 --> 00:11:37.040
Your Highness? Is something wrong?

00:11:37.330 --> 00:11:41.000
I just heard the Voices of the Gods
granted only to those of royal blood.

00:11:41.170 --> 00:11:42.130
Oh, my!

00:11:42.460 --> 00:11:45.880
It must be a blessing from Her Holiness
Lirenna, the Goddess of Light.

00:11:46.210 --> 00:11:48.670
Kobayashi, what does he mean by "Voices of the Gods"?

00:11:48.920 --> 00:11:49.920
I'm not sure.

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:53.250
Some characters can awaken to powers
that let them hear the Voices of the Gods,

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:55.170
but it's way too early for that...

00:11:55.170 --> 00:11:57.460
Endo, did you press any weird buttons?

00:11:57.460 --> 00:11:58.920
Uh, no! I didn't do anything!

00:11:58.920 --> 00:11:59.290
Oh.

00:11:59.290 --> 00:11:59.630
Hmm?

00:11:59.630 --> 00:12:02.130
<b>Siegwald</b>

00:11:59.630 --> 00:12:02.130
<b>Divine gods, shall I address you as</b>

00:11:59.630 --> 00:12:02.130
<b>Lord Endoh and Lady Kobayashee?</b>

00:12:02.380 --> 00:12:03.130
Huh?!

00:12:04.170 --> 00:12:09.170
Divine gods, shall I address you
as Lord Endoh and Lady Kobayashee?

00:12:09.710 --> 00:12:15.670
I am the first-born son of the king of Fitzenhagen,
Crown Prince Siegwald.

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:18.040
I bid you to call me Sieg.

00:12:18.420 --> 00:12:19.170
What?

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:23.750
W-wow! This game has a voice recognition system?!

00:12:24.170 --> 00:12:24.920
It doesn't!

00:12:24.920 --> 00:12:25.580
Huh?

00:12:25.880 --> 00:12:28.880
No, it definitely doesn't feature voice recognition!

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:31.420
Uh? Then how is this happening?

00:12:31.670 --> 00:12:34.670
<b>Siegwald</b>

00:12:31.830 --> 00:12:34.670
<b>I am honored that two divine entities are speaking to me thus.</b>

00:12:32.710 --> 00:12:34.460
O-oh my gosh,

00:12:34.750 --> 00:12:36.170
does he really hear us?

00:12:36.170 --> 00:12:37.170
No way.

00:12:37.170 --> 00:12:38.830
Okay, lemme test it out. Right now!

00:12:38.830 --> 00:12:40.290
How, though?

00:12:40.290 --> 00:12:41.670
Um, let's see...

00:12:42.130 --> 00:12:46.880
Oh! Sieg, if you can really hear what we're saying,

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:51.290
give Liese-tan... I mean, Lieselotte a proper smooch!

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:51.960
"A smooch"?!

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:53.420
What is a "smooch"?

00:12:53.420 --> 00:12:55.080
Also known as a kiss!

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:56.080
A kiss?!

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:57.790
Your Highness?

00:12:57.790 --> 00:12:59.170
Why a smooch?

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:01.710
Th-that was all I could think of!

00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:05.040
Lieselotte may be my fiancée, but...

00:13:05.580 --> 00:13:09.210
No, this is the will of the gods. I must obey.

00:13:09.670 --> 00:13:11.960
We're engaged. A kiss shouldn't be a problem.

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:14.500
But wait, with all these people around...

00:13:15.540 --> 00:13:16.540
Your Highness?

00:13:26.380 --> 00:13:27.750
Y-Your Highness?!

00:13:28.710 --> 00:13:33.920
Oh, her skin is so soft, so fair, so tender...

00:13:34.380 --> 00:13:37.380
Her lips are a glistening pink, too.

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:39.080
Wh-what are you...?

00:13:55.330 --> 00:13:58.210
I... i... i... i...

00:13:58.210 --> 00:14:00.830
It happened!

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:03.460
It happened! It happened! It really happened!

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:04.830
C-calm down, Kobayashi.

00:14:04.830 --> 00:14:06.420
I can't! How can I possibly?!

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:07.830
A kiss! He kissed her!

00:14:06.880 --> 00:14:07.830
Ow!

00:14:07.830 --> 00:14:09.080
Hey, ow, ow, ow! Will you stop?!

00:14:09.080 --> 00:14:11.210
Sieg and Liese-tan kissed!

00:14:11.460 --> 00:14:12.330
On the cheek, but still!

00:14:12.670 --> 00:14:15.880
And jeez, just look at how friggin' cute Liese-tan is!

00:14:16.170 --> 00:14:17.630
"Frig-in cute"?

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:18.500
Hmm?

00:14:25.210 --> 00:14:26.380
What is this?

00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:28.630
How is she so cute?

00:14:29.080 --> 00:14:32.460
Aaah! So cute! She's so cute I just can't!

00:14:30.880 --> 00:14:33.380
I agree! I agree so stop hitting me!

00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:39.670
I had been prepared to receive an icy glare
of disgust or perhaps a slap across the face.

00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:42.670
But of course the gods know well.

00:14:43.290 --> 00:14:45.500
Indeed, just as they say...

00:14:46.210 --> 00:14:49.460
Lieselotte is cute,

00:14:50.580 --> 00:14:51.500
beyond all else.

00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:54.580
Ooh, ow...

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:56.130
I'm not imagining things, am I?

00:14:56.130 --> 00:15:03.170
Yeah, I don't know how, but it looks like we can
communicate with Siegwald, an in-game character.

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:03.790
<b>Siegwald</b>

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:03.790
<b>Will this do, Lady Kobayashee?</b>

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:03.790
Right.

00:15:08.290 --> 00:15:10.170
Maybe we can save her.

00:15:10.500 --> 00:15:11.130
Huh?

00:15:11.330 --> 00:15:13.170
Liese-tan, from death.

00:15:13.170 --> 00:15:14.000
"Death"?

00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:16.670
Yeah. See, Liese-tan dies.

00:15:16.670 --> 00:15:17.170
What?!

00:15:17.170 --> 00:15:19.170
No matter what route you choose.

00:15:20.170 --> 00:15:23.790
When Sieg doesn't love her back,
her sorrow turns to despair,

00:15:24.790 --> 00:15:28.500
and she gets possessed by the dreadful Witch of Yore.

00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:37.210
That transforms her into a hideous monster
and she gets killed.

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:42.460
<b>Love Me</b>

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:42.460
<b>Magically!</b>

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:44.420
That's way too heavy, Magikoi.

00:15:44.420 --> 00:15:48.420
But if we keep communicating with Sieg, then maybe...

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:50.580
...we could help save Lieselotte?

00:15:50.580 --> 00:15:54.960
Yeah. Liese-tan's tragedy can
be averted if Sieg loves her back.

00:15:54.960 --> 00:15:59.960
<b>Siegwald</b>

00:15:54.960 --> 00:15:59.960
<b>Will this do, Lady Kobayashee?</b>

00:15:55.210 --> 00:15:59.960
But if we tell Sieg what's going to happen and
ask him to love her, that wouldn't work.

00:15:59.960 --> 00:16:05.460
I see. So Sieg has to fall in love
with Lieselotte of his own free will.

00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:07.170
That's pretty tricky.

00:16:07.170 --> 00:16:08.580
Let's give it a try, though!

00:16:08.580 --> 00:16:11.210
I want Lieselotte to find her happily ever after!

00:16:11.210 --> 00:16:11.960
Yeah.

00:16:13.380 --> 00:16:14.210
Sieg.

00:16:14.210 --> 00:16:14.920
Yes?

00:16:14.920 --> 00:16:17.750
We have the ability to see your futures.

00:16:17.750 --> 00:16:18.880
Our futures?!

00:16:19.210 --> 00:16:24.670
The way things are, Liese-tan... I mean,
Lieselotte Riefenstahl will face certain doom.

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:26.670
Doom, you say?

00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:31.250
The only one who can save her
from that fate is you, Sieg.

00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:32.920
Me? Is that true?

00:16:33.080 --> 00:16:37.920
From now on, we'll be giving you cues
using running commentary and expert analysis.

00:16:37.920 --> 00:16:39.710
Commentary and analysis?

00:16:39.710 --> 00:16:41.080
So um... I...

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:43.130
I mean, I'm the commentator, Endo.

00:16:41.670 --> 00:16:45.330
<b>Running Commentator: Endo</b>

00:16:43.130 --> 00:16:45.330
And I'm the analyst, Kobayashi!

00:16:43.460 --> 00:16:45.330
<b>Expert Analyst: Kobayashi</b>

00:16:45.750 --> 00:16:49.250
Lord Endoh the Commentator
and Lady Kobayashee the Analyst.

00:16:49.500 --> 00:16:51.710
So they have titles to befit their status.

00:16:52.130 --> 00:16:54.750
Listen to our words to help you out.

00:16:54.750 --> 00:16:58.920
We want you to think for yourself and
really look at Lieselotte properly.

00:17:00.170 --> 00:17:04.080
I promise I will. However, I wish to ask you a few things.

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:05.040
You have questions?

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:05.920
Um, yes.

00:17:06.130 --> 00:17:08.380
Hmm, we shouldn't give any spoilers.

00:17:08.380 --> 00:17:09.000
You're right.

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:09.960
Okay, Sieg.

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:11.460
One question is all you get.

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:13.790
Only one?

00:17:14.130 --> 00:17:18.580
I can only ask one? What should I ask? About the gods?

00:17:18.580 --> 00:17:20.210
About Lieselotte's doom?

00:17:20.420 --> 00:17:22.540
About what's going to happen?

00:17:22.540 --> 00:17:24.710
Aaargh! Wh-what should I ask?

00:17:25.130 --> 00:17:26.920
Okay, so what's your question?

00:17:30.960 --> 00:17:33.710
<b>"What is a</b>

00:17:30.960 --> 00:17:33.710
<b>'tsun de rais'?"</b>

00:17:33.710 --> 00:17:34.630
Oh...

00:17:34.830 --> 00:17:36.210
<b>"Huh?"</b>

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:36.000
Huh?

00:17:37.500 --> 00:17:38.960
I made a mistake.

00:17:40.380 --> 00:17:44.420
That's not it Sieg! Definitely not it, Sieg!

00:17:44.420 --> 00:17:50.670
A tsundere is a person who seems to be all tsun tsun and
prickly, but really just wants to be sweet and affectionate.

00:17:50.670 --> 00:17:52.750
The very definition of Liese-tan, basically.

00:17:52.750 --> 00:17:54.420
Lieselotte?!

00:18:05.170 --> 00:18:07.080
So this is tsun de rais.

00:18:10.630 --> 00:18:13.790
Also, you should know that no one else
can hear us asides from you,

00:18:13.790 --> 00:18:17.000
so you probably look really weird talking to us.

00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:21.040
So going forward, just listen to us talking
but you don't need to respond.

00:18:21.040 --> 00:18:24.080
<b>Siegwald</b>

00:18:21.330 --> 00:18:24.080
<b>Such gracious words! It's much appreciated!</b>

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:23.630
No problem.

00:18:24.250 --> 00:18:26.830
All right, good luck Sieg! Don't you give up, Sieg!

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:30.540
I think the best thing to do here is to have
a friendly study session with all three of you.

00:18:32.170 --> 00:18:33.330
Apologies for the wait.

00:18:33.330 --> 00:18:35.210
My conversation with the gods is over.

00:18:35.710 --> 00:18:39.630
Shall all three of us resume studying this time?

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:41.750
I-is that all right with you, Miss Fiene?

00:18:41.750 --> 00:18:43.000
Huh? Oh, sure!

00:18:43.000 --> 00:18:45.040
So, what part was it you don't understand?

00:18:46.790 --> 00:18:49.540
Umm, right here.

00:18:50.130 --> 00:18:54.210
My, you astound me. You don't even
understand something this elementary?

00:18:54.210 --> 00:18:56.080
Erm...I-I'm sorry.

00:18:56.380 --> 00:18:58.460
Listen well. This is what this means.

00:18:58.460 --> 00:19:03.210
It's just as the gods said. Her attitude may be prickly,

00:18:58.460 --> 00:19:01.000
This is an application of the same thing,

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:04.330
so you just have to think of it the way you did earlier.

00:19:03.830 --> 00:19:05.830
but she's teaching Fiene with such care...

00:19:08.420 --> 00:19:09.420
I see!

00:19:09.630 --> 00:19:10.500
Ah, that there, hmm?

00:19:14.080 --> 00:19:15.630
Lady Lieselotte?

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:22.000
The gods speak the truth.

00:19:22.580 --> 00:19:25.170
Yes, she's very cute indeed.

00:19:29.380 --> 00:19:31.920
Well, I guess it is a little eerie.

00:19:31.920 --> 00:19:35.670
Yeah. The saved data had some weird garbled text,

00:19:36.130 --> 00:19:39.500
and the fact you can't turn off
autoplay mode definitely isn't normal.

00:19:39.500 --> 00:19:42.290
Still, I can't just stop right now.

00:19:42.290 --> 00:19:43.500
I mean, Liese-tan...

00:19:44.170 --> 00:19:45.210
I know!

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:52.080
Huh?

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:53.580
Here, look.

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:55.380
The official fan disc for Magikoi!

00:19:55.380 --> 00:19:56.040
Huh!

00:19:56.540 --> 00:19:59.790
Try playing "Lieselotte's Memoir" included in there.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:02.330
It tells everything there is to know about Liese-tan!

00:20:02.960 --> 00:20:07.290
You'll definitely want to save Liese-tan
after watching that, I swear!

00:20:07.750 --> 00:20:08.630
I'll try it out.

00:20:08.630 --> 00:20:11.630
Let's make sure we give Liese-tan a happy ending!

00:20:11.790 --> 00:20:14.130
With the power of our commentary and analysis!

00:20:14.130 --> 00:20:15.210
Yeah...!

00:20:15.210 --> 00:20:17.920
Although, we'll have to wait for a while.

00:20:18.170 --> 00:20:19.580
Huh? Why? How come?!

00:20:19.580 --> 00:20:21.500
Summer break starts in two days.

00:20:21.960 --> 00:20:24.080
The clubroom will be closed so
we won't be able to play the game.

00:20:24.080 --> 00:20:27.170
N-no waaaaay!

00:20:28.710 --> 00:20:30.210
Y-you're that sad about this?

00:20:30.210 --> 00:20:31.080
I know!

00:20:31.420 --> 00:20:34.290
Endo, come to my house! Let's play it at my house!

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:36.250
Y-your house, Kobayashi?

00:20:36.250 --> 00:20:37.630
Yeah! My house!

00:20:37.830 --> 00:20:40.790
Though maybe you don't wanna have
to see my face over summer break!

00:20:40.790 --> 00:20:42.040
N-no, that's not true!

00:20:42.040 --> 00:20:43.670
Actually, even every day would be-

00:20:43.670 --> 00:20:45.330
Uh, no! Never mind!

00:20:45.710 --> 00:20:51.040
Then let's do it! My parents both work, and my sister's
a college student and she's always out somewhere.

00:20:51.040 --> 00:20:53.080
It's usually just me at home, so it's totally okay!

00:20:53.080 --> 00:20:56.330
Uh, there's nothing okay about what you just said.

00:20:57.420 --> 00:21:00.580
Um, you do realize that I'm a guy, don't you?

00:21:00.580 --> 00:21:01.830
Yeah, of course.

00:21:02.830 --> 00:21:06.080
Our heights, our arms, even our hands
are completely different!

00:21:09.290 --> 00:21:13.580
W...well, if you don't mind, sure.

00:21:13.960 --> 00:21:19.880
All right! Then let's strive for it together—
the best happy end to end all happy ends!

00:21:20.580 --> 00:21:24.960
I guess I can use this summer break to try
and get her to notice me a bit.

00:21:24.960 --> 00:21:27.790
All right! We're gonna give Liese-tan her happy ending!

00:21:27.960 --> 00:21:29.250
C'mon, join me, Endo!

00:21:29.250 --> 00:21:30.210
Yeah...!

00:21:33.790 --> 00:21:35.420
My love is eternal.

00:21:36.580 --> 00:21:40.130
I promise my undying love, to you and only you.

00:21:41.750 --> 00:21:42.670
And, cut!

00:21:42.670 --> 00:21:44.040
Kirise, that was great!

00:21:43.460 --> 00:21:44.540
Just perfect!

00:21:44.540 --> 00:21:45.460
Thank you very much!

00:21:45.460 --> 00:21:46.880
Okay, so this scene...

00:21:46.080 --> 00:21:47.540
Great work, everyone!

00:21:47.040 --> 00:21:48.290
Okay, let's wrap it up.

00:21:48.290 --> 00:21:49.960
Oh, Director! Can I ask you some-

00:21:48.630 --> 00:21:49.960
Hurry, hurry! Yeah, that's right.

00:21:49.960 --> 00:21:50.540
Oh, okay.

00:21:51.420 --> 00:21:52.710
I think it might be better that way.

00:21:53.790 --> 00:21:54.750
It won't be long now.

00:21:55.290 --> 00:21:56.670
Soon enough, I'll get to see you.

00:21:57.460 --> 00:22:05.670
Thanks to the benevolent guidance from the two divine
entities, I was able to make a new discovery today.

00:22:06.290 --> 00:22:07.380
The discovery that...

00:22:08.750 --> 00:22:11.170
Lieselotte is so cute.

00:22:29.420 --> 00:22:31.830
I must strive even harder...

00:22:33.580 --> 00:22:37.670
to become worthy enough to stand by his side!

00:24:14.040 --> 00:24:16.130
Let's make sure we give Liese-tan a happy ending!

00:24:16.130 --> 00:24:18.000
Endo, here's to a long and happy partnership.

00:24:18.000 --> 00:24:19.880
"Partnership"?! Partnership...

00:24:19.880 --> 00:24:20.380
Hmm?

00:24:20.380 --> 00:24:21.130
Uh, no...

00:24:21.130 --> 00:24:22.790
Argh! My heart is pounding!

00:24:22.920 --> 00:24:25.580
Next episode: "The Wand, Maxed Out,
and Favored by the Gods!"

00:24:25.170 --> 00:24:27.960
<b>The Wand, Maxed Out, and Favored by the Gods</b>

00:24:25.580 --> 00:24:26.750
Partnership...!
